{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CrQomhHmPWKNtbufo5Xetq","type":"tool_result","content":"?? docs/reviews/wi-887/004-ADJUDICATE-6e7e50f.md\n?? docs/reviews/wi-887/004-ADJUDICATE-6e7e50f.md.requested\nbrief = combined\nkinds = amendment;first-approval\noutcome = pending\n0 docs/reviews/wi-887/004-ADJUDICATE-6e7e50f.md\n001-REVIEW-A-01ac7b2.md\n002-REVIEW-A-031da17-narrow.md\n003-REVIEW-A-e47a64b-narrow.md\n004-ADJUDICATE-6e7e50f.md\n004-ADJUDICATE-6e7e50f.md.requested\nWI-887-reviewer-retention-final-review.md\n# docs/decisions/wi-887.toml — delegated decisions made in lane wi-887\n# (overnight leg 02, 2026-10-11). Format: project-trajectory/decisions.template.toml.\n\nhigh_risk = [\"D-001\"]\n\n[decision.D-001]\ndecided = \"Done-when's 'the gate's evidence that a verdict came from the final reviewer's scope is the verdict file itself, under WI-884's filing contract' is read as WI-884's whole filing contract, which already binds the coordinator-written `# review-scope:` and `# session-gen:` records in the committed session log (WI-884 D-004). Round 1's fix (plan R1, answering review 001's F1) adds a distinct final kind to that existing `# review-scope:` record and has the gate read that one binding, with the mode resolved from both dials (retention on and final_reviewer persisted) in one reader. The new session-mode and keep-scope columns stay audit-only. The reviewer-written round text is not used as provenance: a reviewer cannot attest where its own session came from.\"\nalternative = \"Read 'the verdict file itself' as the round file's own text, and have the reviewer write its scope into it; or amend the Done-when wording first under a bound verdict.\"\nreversal_cost = \"Medium: an overrule moves the binding from the session log header to the round file, rewriting the gate reader and its tests before landing.\"\nwhy_not_escalated = \"It applies the spec's own pointer to WI-884's contract, adds no authority beyond the record the gate already reads, and the checkpoint sitting judges the rows that state it; the lane's Done-when text is unchanged.\"\nreview = \"\"\n\n[decision.D-002]\ndecided = \"The two upward size re-stamps (agent_loop.py 2408 -> 2416, then 2418 and 2427 in the fix rounds; agent_common.py 1051 -> 1053) are accepted as reviewed bumps with their reasons in the ratchet, as the ratchet's long record of reviewed bumps allows for modules already past the threshold; no verbatim helper move was made to net them to zero.\"\nalternative = \"Move a pure helper verbatim out of each module (WI-884 D-009's pattern) so neither grows.\"\nreversal_cost = \"Low: a later verbatim move can re-stamp both down.\"\nwhy_not_escalated = \"Neither module is pushed past the threshold by this change; both were past it already, and the growth is the spec's own wiring and log columns.\"\nreview = \"\"\n\n[decision.D-003]\ndecided = \"Reviews in this lane run on Codex gpt-6.1-sol at medium: the signed-in account offers it again (probed 2026-10-10 22:40 local), so coordinator-2026-10-10 D-017's Luna substitution no longer applies.\"\nalternative = \"Keep reviewing on gpt-6-luna at high for continuity with leg 01.\"\nreversal_cost = \"Low.\"\nwhy_not_escalated = \"It restores the owner's named reviewer.\"\nreview = \"\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d52360a6-7377-4d1e-a658-4cbc4052baa8","uuid":"e58aa685-f40e-46df-8b02-22814aa43f29","timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:16:41.835Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"?? docs/reviews/wi-887/004-ADJUDICATE-6e7e50f.md\n?? docs/reviews/wi-887/004-ADJUDICATE-6e7e50f.md.requested\nbrief = combined\nkinds = amendment;first-approval\noutcome = pending\n0 docs/reviews/wi-887/004-ADJUDICATE-6e7e50f.md\n001-REVIEW-A-01ac7b2.md\n002-REVIEW-A-031da17-narrow.md\n003-REVIEW-A-e47a64b-narrow.md\n004-ADJUDICATE-6e7e50f.md\n004-ADJUDICATE-6e7e50f.md.requested\nWI-887-reviewer-retention-final-review.md\n# docs/decisions/wi-887.toml — delegated decisions made 