{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv3Z4Euj5qqMGBJhBdy6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've recorded the verdict as commit `2604dc8e0` (trailer `WI: WI-887`). No act followed it, and no registry cell, `Status` or approval snapshot changed.\n\n**Amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=13`.** Every amended row adds a behaviour, admission or verification clause the approved text didn't have.\n\n- **I would bless 8 as they stand:** SR-154, SR-156, LLR-045, LLR-262, LLR-269, LLR-270, LLR-305, TC-322.\n- **5 go back:**\n  - **SR-227:**\n    - The reviewer obligations sit inside the sentence that opens \"Where the declared *adjudicator* retention dial…\". Read literally, they only apply when the adjudicator dial is on, and they bind \"adjudication content\" rather than the loop's reviewer.\n    - Its acceptance criteria say the review log's reviewed range is \"audit data that no gate or scheduler reads\". The gate does read that range (`# review-scope:`), and the same criteria rely on it for the final-round admission. Only the `session-mode` and `keep-scope` columns are audit-only.\n    - A \".;\" splice in the Requirement.\n    - The Rationale should cite lane decision D-001, which this wording depends on and which is still pending you.\n  - **LLR-140 and LLR-207:** each cell gained a new sentence admitting the persisted final round, but the old \"only a fresh full scope gates\" sentence was left in place. Each cell now states two admission sets that disagree.\n  - **TC-205:** its Expected cell still says retained-session rounds hold the gate, while it now also lets a persisted final round gate, which is a retained session.\n  - **TC-266:** the rewrite dropped verification clauses that were already approved: at dial zero the runner version isn't read, the launch equals a fresh session's, and no keep-warm is built. No other test case now states them. The tests themselves still exist.\n\n**First approval: `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=1`.** TC-351's Expected claims \"audit fields grant no gate authority\", but none of its 21 cited tests checks that. They only show the columns get written. That claim also rests on SR-227's wording, which goes back too.\n\n**The re-attestation act can't happen in this sitting.** Each of the three registries holds a row I'm returning, so none can be re-anchored. I ran the snapshot for the eight rows I'd bless and it refused, naming SR-227, LLR-140, LLR-207, TC-205 and TC-266. It wrote nothing.\n\n**Where the corrective work is:** the follow-up drafts are under `## Dispositions` in each section of the verdict file, not in the WI-887 spec. Intake only mints drafts from adjudication-class specs and WI-887 is an ordinary one, so drafts there would never be minted. The coordinator-cycle skill routes returned spine text in a lane checkpoint back to the lane's spine author (Terra) instead. Every fix is a text change; no code needs to change.\n\n**Next sitting:** once the six returned rows are reworked, re-sit them together with the eight blessable rows. One act can then anchor all three registries, including TC-351's approval.\n\nThe `.requested` binding file is still untracked; I left it for the coordinator's bookkeeping."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":973,"cache_read_input_tokens":182535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":973},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d52360a6-7377-4d1e-a658-4cbc4052baa8","uuid":"2460a7dd-3eea-41d1-b664-0b33947c83ed","timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:20:33.759Z","request_id":"req_011Cfv3Z3zHm4FcRFSqVLnXo"}
